8f-4361-5ebf-99b7-4f21bd7e90b7" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309519 1145 "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $5x-4y=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨5,-4,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $4y-5z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,4,-5⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨5,-4,0⟩\\times ⟨0,4,-5⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -5\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =20i+25j+20k \\\\  & =⟨20,25,20⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309521 13194139534776 true] [17592186309520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309522 13194139534776 true] [17592186309520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309523 13194139534776 true] [17592186309520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309524 13194139534776 true] [17592186309520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309525 13194139534776 true] [17592186309520 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534776 true] [17592186309520 1041 "selection" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309520 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309522 13194139534776 true] [17592186309520 1110 #uuid "887dd48c-ca9b-539c-a987-adbe261b4e19" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309521 1034 "⟨4,-5,0⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309521 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309521 1111 #uuid "5b0ce8b6-6dbe-5dea-9b88-5729aa59ac33" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309522 1034 "⟨20,25,20⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309522 1111 #uuid "2a2d6712-803b-5fda-86ca-914e95f9f438" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309523 1034 "⟨0,1,-5⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309523 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309523 1111 #uuid "3b15c3cb-3433-5846-8d12-1c834085ece6" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309524 1034 "⟨0,0,-9⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309524 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309524 1111 #uuid "147e4708-d07d-5614-ae6d-4ca7d55b1f0f" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309525 1034 "⟨5,-4,0⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309525 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309525 1111 #uuid "f7ec77c1-ae66-5a52-b343-ea088b631874" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309526 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309527 13194139534776 true] [17592186309526 1089 "q-71268" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309526 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534776 true] [17592186309526 1100 "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $z=1$ and $x=y.$" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309526 1113 #uuid "ce5171f6-22a8-5be0-9547-0d96404368c9" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309526 1145 "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $z=1$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,0,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x=y$ (or $x-y=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨0,0,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+j \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309527 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309528 13194139534776 true] [17592186309527 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309529 13194139534776 true] [17592186309527 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309530 13194139534776 true] [17592186309527 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309531 13194139534776 true] [17592186309527 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309532 13194139534776 true] [17592186309527 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534776 true] [17592186309527 1041 "selection" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309527 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309530 13194139534776 true] [17592186309527 1110 #uuid "3e29a774-9bd2-54dd-8c69-555bcacd95c9" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309528 1034 "⟨1,-1,0⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309528 1111 #uuid "39d3777c-931e-54be-bc36-4a01094158c2" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309529 1034 "⟨0,0,1⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309529 1111 #uuid "2976cdff-3ec8-5aeb-9e6f-7febfe55f031" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309530 1034 "⟨1,1,0⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309530 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309530 1111 #uuid "823c751c-6086-558b-a81f-7377b09e6e53" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309531 1034 "⟨-1,0,0⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309531 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309531 1111 #uuid "570af63d-4fcd-572a-8beb-b6e23ef63681" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309532 1034 "⟨0,1,-1⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309532 1111 #uuid "3d216364-6877-5cf5-b473-f039b81e2723" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309533 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309534 13194139534776 true] [17592186309533 1089 "q-71347" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309533 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534776 true] [17592186309533 1100 "The intersection of the planes $2x-y+6=0$ and $y+2z-2=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},0,{a}_{3}⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}-{a}_{3},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309533 1113 #uuid "b23b0cec-a767-5778-8e67-5c10a6b25080" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309533 1145 "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $y=0.$ Substituting this to the first equation gives \n\n$$\n2x-0+6=0\\,⟹\\,x=-3,\n$$\n\nand substituting $y=0$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n0+2z-2=0\\,⟹\\,z=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x-y+6=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $y+2z-2=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,2⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2i-4j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-4,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨-2,-4,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}-{a}_{3}=-3-1=-4,$ and $b=⟨-2,-4,2⟩.$" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309535 13194139534776 true] [17592186309534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309536 13194139534776 true] [17592186309534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309537 13194139534776 true] [17592186309534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309538 13194139534776 true] [17592186309534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309539 13194139534776 true] [17592186309534 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534776 true] [17592186309534 1041 "selection" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309534 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309538 13194139534776 true] [17592186309534 1110 #uuid "49d55ebd-d47b-5681-8adf-7c27083248c7" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309535 1034 "{a}_{1}-{a}_{3}=2,\\,b=⟨-4,2,2⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309535 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309535 1111 #uuid "ca85272d-c8e6-5de8-ae5f-276509834959" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309536 1034 "{a}_{1}-{a}_{3}=3,\\,b=⟨-4,2,2⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309536 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309536 1111 #uuid "a56f4364-17c3-5089-86db-c35c7232a8ea" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309537 1034 "{a}_{1}-{a}_{3}=-2,\\,b=⟨-4,2,2⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309537 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309537 1111 #uuid "60692775-03e2-554e-a6c2-463e42103a5b" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309538 1034 "{a}_{1}-{a}_{3}=-4,\\,b=⟨-2,-4,2⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309538 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309538 1111 #uuid "2a60b638-d8b1-57b4-b880-3bd292690ba1" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309539 1034 "{a}_{1}-{a}_{3}=3,\\,b=⟨-2,-4,2⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309539 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309539 1111 #uuid "0eb7bccb-6b13-538d-a7d9-6876fef93242" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309540 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309541 13194139534776 true] [17592186309540 1089 "q-71447" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309540 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534776 true] [17592186309540 1100 "The intersection of the planes $x+2y-4z+6=0$ and $x-4y+2z=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨0,{a}_{2},{a}_{3}⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{2}+{a}_{3},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309540 1113 #uuid "65aeb577-5179-51b6-b6d7-0edba5765814" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309540 1145 "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $x=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n0-4y+2z=0\\,⟹\\,z=2y,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x=0$ and $z=2y$ into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y-4z+6 & =0 \\\\ 0+2y-4(2y)+6 & =0 \\\\ -6y & =-6 \\\\ y & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $z=2y=2$ and $a=⟨0,1,2⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $x+2y-4z+6=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,2,-4⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-4y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-4,2⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,2,-4⟩\\times ⟨1,-4,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-12i-6j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-12,-6,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can pick any vector that is parallel to ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}$ as a direction vector of the line. So, let \n \n\n$$\nb=-\\frac{1}{6}({n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2})=⟨2,1,1⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨0,1,2⟩+t⟨2,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=1+2=3,$ and $b=⟨2,1,1⟩.$" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309541 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309542 13194139534776 true] [17592186309541 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309543 13194139534776 true] [17592186309541 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309544 13194139534776 true] [17592186309541 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309545 13194139534776 true] [17592186309541 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309546 13194139534776 true] [17592186309541 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534776 true] [17592186309541 1041 "selection" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309541 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309546 13194139534776 true] [17592186309541 1110 #uuid "2f7522a2-8365-5bbe-a942-7e6cfc58e6e1" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309542 1034 "{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=-3,\\,b=⟨2,1,3⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309542 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309542 1111 #uuid "3574aa75-7514-5202-b4e9-949399ecaa1e" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309543 1034 "{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=2,\\,b=⟨2,2,1⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309543 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309543 1111 #uuid "99ea64db-fa3c-5995-a6f1-668a9a79a49c" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309544 1034 "{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=6,\\,b=⟨1,3,6⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309544 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309544 1111 #uuid "ac61c71e-c9b1-518c-9f17-bc751449a034" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309545 1034 "{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=-2,\\,b=⟨2,1,2⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309545 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309545 1111 #uuid "1dc437d3-cdd7-512b-925b-8d2c6cd42861" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309546 1034 "{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=3,\\,b=⟨2,1,1⟩" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309546 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534776 true] [17592186309546 1111 #uuid "bed335ac-6bd0-574b-bda3-8d868ba09685" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309547 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309548 13194139534776 true] [17592186309547 1089 "q-71456" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309547 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534776 true] [17592186309547 1100 "Given the two planes $x-3y+z=0$ and $2x-y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,5,2⟩.$\n- The planes intersect on a line.\n- The planes are coincident." 13194139534776 true] [17592186309547 1113 #uuid "4895b4d9-6e99-5443-b10a-85bc7b1b4155" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309547 1145 "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-3y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-3,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x-y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,-1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-3,1⟩\\times ⟨2,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+2j+5k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,5⟩\\ne ⟨1,5,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes cannot be coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." 13194139534776 true] [17592186309548 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309549 13194139534776 true] [17592186309548 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309550 13194139534776 true] [17592186309548 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309551 13194139534776 true] [17592186309548 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309552 13194139534776 true] [17592186309548 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309553 13194139534776 true] [17592186309548 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534776 true] [17592186309548 1041 "selection" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309548 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309553 13194139534776 true] [17592186309548 1110 #uuid "2f73c74d-d549-5390-8101-8d61fca29ba6" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309549 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309549 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534776 true] [17592186309