\\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}=0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are parallel. Hence, the corresponding planes are also parallel. So, the planes can't intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed,  the second plane passes through the origin  $O(0,0,0)$ but the first plane doesn't: \n\n$$\n2(0)-4(0)+6(0)+2=2\\ne 0\n$$\n\n So, the planes can't be coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." 13194139534776 true] [17592186309555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309556 13194139534776 true] [17592186309555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309557 13194139534776 true] [17592186309555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309558 13194139534776 true] [17592186309555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309559 13194139534776 true] [17592186309555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309560 13194139534776 true] [17592186309555 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534776 true] [17592186309555 1041 "selection" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309555 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309558 13194139534776 true] [17592186309555 1110 #uuid "d3652218-a27d-5c9d-9f9c-1185dc023fdf" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309556 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534776 true] [17592186309556 1111 #uuid "4a9f90ff-04ab-56f3-a990-b883575306c6" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309557 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534776 true] [17592186309557 1111 #uuid "c446fdfd-caf2-5a5e-ab87-c16c8089c4ec" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309558 1034 "I only" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534776 true] [17592186309558 1111 #uuid "c7c67c65-8b86-54b4-97dc-1f02d1fcef4b" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309559 1034 "III only" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309559 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534776 true] [17592186309559 1111 #uuid "13f99e1d-6f89-5603-aace-967a83531901" 13194139534776 true] [17592186309560 1034 "II only" 13194139534776 true] [1759218630956